{"tool_name":"paralyzer","contents":["bioconda","biocontainers","bioschemas","biotools","galaxy","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:paralyzer","bioconda:paralyzer","galaxy:paralyzer"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"paralyzer","version":"1.5","home":"https://ohlerlab.mdc-berlin.de/software/PARalyzer_85/","license":"PARalyzer is provided for academic use only, if you wish to use it in another setting please contact Uwe Ohler.","summary":"We developed the PARalyzer algorithm to generate a high resolution map of interaction sites between RNA-binding proteins and their targets. The algorithm utilizes the deep sequencing reads generated by PAR-CLIP (Photoactivatable-Ribonucleoside-Enhanced Crosslinking and Immunoprecipitation) protocol.The use of photoactivatable nucleotides in the PAR-CLIP protocol results in more efficient crosslinking between the RNA-binding protein and its target relative to other CLIP methods; in addition a nucleotide substitution occurs at the site of crosslinking, providing for single-nucleotide resolution binding information. PARalyzer utilizes this nucleotide substition in a kernel density estimate classifier to generate the high resolution set of Protein-RNA interaction sites.","identifiers":["biotools:paralyzer"],"build":{"noarch":"generic","number":3},"requirements":{"build":["openjdk"],"run":["openjdk"]},"source_url":"https://ohlerlab.mdc-berlin.de/files/duke/PARalyzer/PARalyzer_v1_5.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["PARalyzer 2G"]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"paralyzer","identifiers":["biotools:paralyzer","doi:10.1186/gb-2011-12-8-r79"],"license":"PARalyzer is provided for academic use only, if you wish to use it in another setting please contact Uwe Ohler.","summary":"Tool to analyze cross-linking and immunoprecipitation data (clip)","home_url":"https://ohlerlab.mdc-berlin.de/software/PARalyzer_85/","keywords":["Argonaute Proteins","Binding Sites","Databases, Genetic","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Immunoprecipitation","Li